# Desk app direction - rollback of Claude setup detour
date: 2026-10-31
who: Codex Prime
state: Director-directed rollback; existing workflow remains in use

## Director instruction
> Well that is fucking useless then.  So we need to roll this back.  Please forgive my language but if it breaks everything done.  how is this helpful?

## What is withdrawn
The separate Claude-room assignment 0001, mandatory isolation preflight, execution
hold introduced by this setup, Chat-and-ZIP workaround and separate-room return
route are withdrawn. No sandbox migration is required to continue the existing
project workflow. Do not treat any of those proposals as a new boot requirement.
The room is inactive reference/history, not an assignment or return destination.

## What continues
Use the established lib-build work book, released page-local packs, designated
return captures, evidence and Prime review. Preserve existing recording and Git
publication procedures. Do not infer a new return address from this rollback:
the released pack specifies it. No manual file carrying is introduced.
Claude remains available for design, Colab and bounded labs under explicit packs.
This rollback does not authorize unrelated production changes or resume a
completed prior build. Existing holds, including AR-01, remain in force.

## App priority retained
Build the smallest usable core that records an assignment, lets a worker retrieve
it, accepts its durable return and evidence, lets Prime retrieve and review it,
and preserves the next action across restart. Use the existing workflow while
developing its replacement. Demonstrate it for the current Prime first.
Candidate construction and approval-controlled application remain the broader
goal; do not require the entire future system before the first handoff works.
Design discussion and Colab precede implementation. Prime prepares bounded
implementation packs; Grok builds. No new implementation is released by this note.

## Next action
Prepare the app-core integration design assignment through the existing work-book
pack/return route. Review the outstanding Claude 0518 return independently; do
not lose it or treat it as accepted merely because the development priority changed.

